WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.040
JENNY BROWN: Welcome back
to Cloud Storage Bytes.

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:04.900
Now that you've got
the billing basics,

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:07.200
let's add a level
of complexity, like

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:10.440
when a client needs to
be billed for their usage

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:12.720
of your resources.

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:14.310
Today on Cloud
Storage Bytes, we'll

00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:16.620
take you into the world
of Requester Pays.

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:18.452
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:24.380
Whenever a user accesses
a Cloud Storage resource,

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:26.240
like a bucket or
an object, there

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:29.300
are charges associated with
both making and executing

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:30.560
the request.

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:33.050
This includes operation
charges for performing

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:36.410
a request, network charges
for reading the data,

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:38.420
and data retrieval
charges if the data

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:42.080
is stored as nearline
storage or coldline storage.

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:45.530
Now, normally the project
owner of the resource

00:00:45.530 --> 00:00:47.810
is billed for these
access charges.

00:00:47.810 --> 00:00:50.390
But this isn't
always appropriate.

00:00:50.390 --> 00:00:52.400
If the requester provides
a billing project

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:54.800
with their request,
the requester's project

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:56.720
can be billed instead.

00:00:56.720 --> 00:00:58.460
And this feature
is appropriately

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:00.650
called Requester Pays.

00:01:00.650 --> 00:01:03.480
With Requester Pays
enabled on your bucket,

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:06.350
you can require requesters
to include a billing project

00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:10.010
in their request, thus billing
the requester's project.

00:01:10.010 --> 00:01:12.240
Enabling Requester
Pays is useful.

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:14.390
For example, if you
have a lot of data

00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:16.980
that you want to make
available to your users,

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:20.670
but you don't want to be charged
for their access of that data.

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:22.850
Note that there are some
charges that are always

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:25.880
going to be applied to the
project containing the bucket,

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:28.400
even when Requester
Pays is enabled.

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:30.980
These charges include
storage charges

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:34.880
for storing data in a bucket and
any applicable early deletion

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:35.900
charges.

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:38.300
For complete details
on those caveats,

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:40.980
go ahead and check out
the docs linked below.

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:45.020
And now, let's look into how
to enable Requester Pays.

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:47.120
Start in the Cloud
Storage browser

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:49.760
in the Google Cloud
Platform Console.

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:51.890
In the list of buckets,
find the bucket

00:01:51.890 --> 00:01:53.420
that you want to
enable and click

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:56.420
the Off button in the
Requester Pays column.

00:01:56.420 --> 00:01:59.360
In the window that
appears, click Enable.

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:01.970
Once enabled, a
green bubble and On

00:02:01.970 --> 00:02:05.660
will appear in the Requester
Pays column for that bucket.

00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:08.389
Of course, once you
enable Requester Pays,

00:02:08.389 --> 00:02:10.229
you may need to disable it.

00:02:10.229 --> 00:02:12.860
So let's walk through
that process as well.

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:15.260
To disable Requester
Pays on a bucket,

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:18.320
go ahead and start in the Cloud
Storage browser in the Google

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:20.320
Cloud Platform Console.

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:22.280
In the list of buckets,
find the bucket

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:25.240
you want to disable and click
the On button in the Requester

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:26.480
Pays column.

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:29.570
In the window that
appears, click Disable.

00:02:29.570 --> 00:02:32.270
Once disabled, a
gray bubble and Off

00:02:32.270 --> 00:02:34.880
will appear in the
Requester Pays column.

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:38.000
To check whether Requester
Pays is enabled on a bucket,

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:40.370
take a look at the
list of buckets.

00:02:40.370 --> 00:02:42.560
The Requester Pays
status of each bucket

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:45.450
is found in that
Requester Pays column.

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:47.900
So we've looked at how
to enable and disable

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:50.540
Requester Pays on your
own storage buckets.

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:52.550
But what if you're
on the other side?

00:02:52.550 --> 00:02:54.050
What if you're the
account who wants

00:02:54.050 --> 00:02:58.280
to access an object stored
in a Requester Pays bucket?

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:00.260
Let's check out
accessing Requester Pays

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:02.540
buckets using gsutil.

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:04.490
Here's how to include
a billing project

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:07.340
that you can download an object
stored in a Requester Pays

00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:09.120
bucket.

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:12.750
Project ID is the ID of
the project to be billed.

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:16.170
For example, my-project.

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:19.500
Bucket name is the name
of the relevant bucket.

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:23.270
For example, my-bucket.

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:26.720
Object name is the name of the
object you want to download.

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:30.760
For example, pets/dog.

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:33.040
Object destination
is the location where

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:35.170
you want to save your object.

00:03:35.170 --> 00:03:38.650
For example, desktop/dog.

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:41.920
Keep in mind that buckets that
have Requester Pays disabled

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:44.740
still accept requests that
include a billing project.

00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:47.590
And charges are applied to
the billing project supplied

00:03:47.590 --> 00:03:48.790
in the request.

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:51.340
So make sure you consider
any billing implications

00:03:51.340 --> 00:03:53.770
prior to including a
billing project in any

00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:55.510
of your requests.

00:03:55.510 --> 00:03:57.400
There's more to come
